.SS "template<class T> bool csmp::binaryFileRead (std::fstream & fp, std::deque< std::vector< T > > & stl_ctner)"
Reads a vector of STL vector data from a binary file\&. The STL container is erased before adding the data, if it already contained any data\&. How many records are read is specified by an 'unsigned long' number which precedes the dataset\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
A pointer to a binary file opened in read binary mode ("rb"), and a reference to an STL vector of vector\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
returns the boolean 'true' if the number of data records which precedes the dataset in the file has been read correctly\&. If the file pointer is invalid or less data are read, the function returns false\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
Uses the ANSI C function fread()\&. The vector<\fBvector<T>\fP > which will hold the data is erased if it is not empty\&. Storage is reserved for the new number of elements which is read from file\&. Then the elements are read and the container is returned\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
Efficiently read data into STL vector of vectors\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
The function will return false if (1) the file pointer is invalid, (2) the number of data records cannot be read correctly, and (3) if this number does not match the number of records which were actually read\&. 
