.SS "double csmp::delta_X_FromFV_Volume (double FV_volume, uint32_t dim)"
Calculates the critical tranport distance in the direction of flow delta x from the volume of the finite-volume cell under the assumption that the FV cell is spherical\&. For this case this distance is equivalent to the diameter of the sphere d = 2 (3 V / 4 pi)^1/3 where V is the FV volume\&.

.PP
For skewed elements this method may fail, but it should give a rather conservative estimate for the case where the element is elongated in the direction of the flow\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The method needs the volume of the current FV cell as input\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The method returns the diameter of the hypothetically spherical FV cell\&. 
.RE
.PP

