.SS "bool csmp::doesDomainsFileExist (const char * regions_file)"

.PP
read regions from file ReduceToDomains() reads an ASCII (text) input file to determine the names of the model regions that shall be retained by the current model toopology\&. The name of the input file is created from the user supplied character string by appending '-regions\&.txt'\&.

.PP
The regions file consists of the following:

.PP
.IP "1." 4
headline with file name, model name etc\&.
.IP "2." 4
properties whose specific values shall be listed after region name (here the tab key separates the property names which can contain whitespace)\&. At least, the property 'permeability' must be specified\&.
.PP

.PP
If the file is used only to identify the regions of interest, the second line and the property information in the later part of the file will be ignored\&. Still the second line is treated as if it would contain property data\&. No region names can be specified in it\&. We recommend to write 'no property data' into the second line to clarify if the file is only used to select output regions\&.

.PP
.IP "3." 4
model regions followed by property values (after the last property value in each line, arbitrary comments can be placed but will be ignored)
.PP

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIregions_file\fP The name of the regions file for which an extension '-regions\&.txt' is appended\&. 
.br
.RE
.PP
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
This method does not recognize the standard comments yet\&. Thus, if you put # in front of an item the method will still read the line and try to interpret the following input\&. 
.br
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
In conjunction with input of mesh topologies such as ANSYS or FRED derived meshes\&. 
.br
.SH "Messages"
.PP
The method reports if the input file cannot be opened or if one of the target regions is not contained in the model topology\&. In the latter case a ERROR is raised\&. 
