.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void csmp::randomPerturb (\fBModel\fP< dim > & sg, const char * prop, double by_percent_of_max_value)"

.PP
using random number generator, adds percentage of Gaussian noise to variable values Randomly perturbs the values of a scalar target property by subtracting an amount which varies between minus zero and the specified percentage of the original maximum value of the target property\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
RandomPerturb() requires the name of the property which shall be perturbed and the percentage of the original maximum value of the property by which the property shall be perturbed, in order to operate\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
Processes which are critically dependent on initial conditions can profit from a 'noisy' input signal when one tries to simulate natural behaviour\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
RandomPerturb() only handles scalar variables and it will therefore report an error and return without executing when one tries to perturb a vector or tensor variable\&. 
