.RS 4
returns error code or zero if all data records were read successfully\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "template<uint32_t dim> bool csmp::readBoundaryPropertyConditions (\fBModel\fP< dim > & model, std::ifstream & ifs, char * text_line, size_t line_length, bool verbose)"

.PP
read boundary conditions reads the 'property flags assigned to boundary' (fifth config file data block) from file and assigns the resulting property flags in the target region\&. The format of any entry in the data block should have the form\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
# regionname        qualifier           input property          target flag
BOUNDARY3   (tab)       interior    (tab)   fluid pressure  (tab)   Dirichlet
.fi
.PP

.PP
The target flag is the one that will be assigned to variables of the target type in the boundary identified by name\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
A reference to the current \fBModel\fP object and the line of text that contains the boundary property flag information\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
The method reports the data that are read from file to stdout and reports any possible parsing errors\&. 
